# P3 phase acceptance (ADR 0018 §7): a bad termination is measurable and heats. The lamp circuit
# (lamp-circuit.console, at Journeyman) with the breaker's load screw at 20 % of its marked torque, plus
# the D12 120 V 1500 W heater on the junction box's splices: the lamp and the heater draw about 12.84 A
# through the loose screw for 600 s of sim time (the hot spot, tau about 30 s, and the conductors reach
# their steady state). The same commands as bad-termination.ts; apps/sim-cli/src/bad-termination.spec.ts
# pins BAD_TERMINATION_HASH and BAD_TERMINATION_SNAPSHOT_HASH and derives every expectation from the
# built circuit's current. Its save is the frozen fixture
# libs/domain/save-format/fixtures/v4/ctrl/bad-termination-engine-7-catalog-3.ctrl (--save).
#   pnpm sim run apps/sim-cli/scenarios/bad-termination.console --world content/levels/workshop.json --difficulty journeyman
# 1. The split-phase stand-in supply (D12; P4's service and load centre replace it), headless, to the
#    left of the panel.
entity.place --inEntry null --mountedOn null --orientationMdeg.pitch 0 --orientationMdeg.roll 0 --orientationMdeg.yaw 0 --positionMm.x -1500 --positionMm.y 300 --positionMm.z 0 --ref.id utility.larkmoor-split-phase-25kva --ref.version 1
# 2. The DIN panel hung on the stud faces (as in nm-cable-run); two bottom knockouts knocked out with
#    the screwdriver's blade: ko-bottom-1 for the supply conductors, ko-bottom-2 for the NM-B.
entity.place --inEntry null --mountedOn null --orientationMdeg.pitch 0 --orientationMdeg.roll 0 --orientationMdeg.yaw 0 --positionMm.x -1010 --positionMm.y 800 --positionMm.z -21 --ref.id panel.pellmoor-din-400x500 --ref.version 1
enclosure.openEntry --entry ko-bottom-1 --id 2 --tool.id tool.veltmark-sd-2 --tool.version 1
enclosure.openEntry --entry ko-bottom-2 --id 2 --tool.id tool.veltmark-sd-2 --tool.version 1
# 3. The 15 A breaker on rail 1 (entity 3, labelled CB1 with the label printer); two feed-through
#    blocks (4 line, 5 neutral) and a ground block (6) on rail 2. Positions are placeInWorld's for the
#    script's cursor points.
entity.place --inEntry null --mountedOn.entity 2 --mountedOn.mount rail-1 --orientationMdeg.pitch 0 --orientationMdeg.roll 0 --orientationMdeg.yaw 0 --positionMm.x -940 --positionMm.y 1105 --positionMm.z 1 --ref.id breaker.saltmere-1p-15a --ref.version 1
entity.place --inEntry null --mountedOn.entity 2 --mountedOn.mount rail-2 --orientationMdeg.pitch 0 --orientationMdeg.roll 0 --orientationMdeg.yaw 0 --positionMm.x -819 --positionMm.y 951 --positionMm.z 1 --ref.id tb.quennick-st4 --ref.version 1
entity.place --inEntry null --mountedOn.entity 2 --mountedOn.mount rail-2 --orientationMdeg.pitch 0 --orientationMdeg.roll 0 --orientationMdeg.yaw 0 --positionMm.x -813 --positionMm.y 951 --positionMm.z 1 --ref.id tb.quennick-st4 --ref.version 1
entity.place --inEntry null --mountedOn.entity 2 --mountedOn.mount rail-2 --orientationMdeg.pitch 0 --orientationMdeg.roll 0 --orientationMdeg.yaw 0 --positionMm.x -807 --positionMm.y 951 --positionMm.z 1 --ref.id tb.quennick-pe4 --ref.version 1
entity.label --id 3 --text CB1 --tool.id tool.penmarrow-lp-12 --tool.version 1
# 4. Make up the panel: the black THHN jumper (wire 1) from the breaker's load screw to the line
#    block's top clamp. THE BAD TERMINATION: the breaker screw (end a) set to 0.8 N.m, 20 % of its
#    marked 4 N.m, on the 0.3-1.2 N.m torque screwdriver (+/-6 %: this landing draws 0.8127 N.m,
#    r = 0.2032, the loose-clamp regime, about 82 x R0). The block end at its 0.6 N.m.
wire.add --a.entity 3 --a.terminal load --a.termination.accessory null --a.termination.clamp.tool.id tool.calderyn-ts-03 --a.termination.clamp.tool.version 1 --a.termination.clamp.torqueNm 0.8 --a.termination.method screw --a.termination.strip.hole sol14 --a.termination.strip.lengthMm 13 --a.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-1018 --a.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --b.entity 4 --b.terminal a --b.termination.accessory null --b.termination.clamp.tool.id tool.calderyn-ts-03 --b.termination.clamp.tool.version 1 --b.termination.clamp.torqueNm 0.6 --b.termination.method screw --b.termination.strip.hole sol14 --b.termination.strip.lengthMm 9 --b.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-1018 --b.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --colour.base black --colour.stripe null --lengthMm 157 --ref.id conductor.tallowmere-thhn-14-solid --ref.version 1 --route [] --tool.id tool.veltmark-dc-8 --tool.version 1
# 5. The junction box (7) against stud 4 and the lamp box (8) against stud 6's left face; the clamps
#    the cables use opened with the screwdriver.
entity.place --inEntry null --mountedOn null --orientationMdeg.pitch 0 --orientationMdeg.roll 0 --orientationMdeg.yaw 0 --positionMm.x -835 --positionMm.y -850 --positionMm.z -21 --ref.id box.tinmoor-2g-nm --ref.version 1
entity.place --inEntry null --mountedOn null --orientationMdeg.pitch 0 --orientationMdeg.roll 0 --orientationMdeg.yaw 0 --positionMm.x -165 --positionMm.y -850 --positionMm.z -21 --ref.id box.tinmoor-2g-nm --ref.version 1
enclosure.openEntry --entry clamp-top-1 --id 7 --tool.id tool.veltmark-sd-2 --tool.version 1
enclosure.openEntry --entry clamp-bottom-1 --id 7 --tool.id tool.veltmark-sd-2 --tool.version 1
enclosure.openEntry --entry clamp-bottom-1 --id 8 --tool.id tool.veltmark-sd-2 --tool.version 1
# 6. Cable 1 (wires 2 black, 3 white, 4 bare): the panel's ko-bottom-2 -> two staples down stud 4 ->
#    the junction box's top clamp. Cable 2 (wires 5, 6, 7): the junction box's bottom clamp -> a staple
#    on stud 4 -> a hole bored through stud 5 with the 3/4 in ship auger -> a staple on stud 6 -> the
#    lamp box's bottom clamp. Staples within 304.8 mm of each box and 1371.6 mm of each other (NFPA 70
#    Art. 334.30 by number); cut with the diagonal cutters at routeDefaultLengthMm.
cable.add --a.entity 2 --a.entry ko-bottom-2 --b.entity 7 --b.entry clamp-top-1 --lengthMm 2303 --ref.id cable.sorrelby-nmb-14-2 --ref.version 1 --route [{"entity":null,"fixture":"stud-wall","kind":"staple","positionMm":{"x":-835,"y":600,"z":-65},"tool":null},{"entity":null,"fixture":"stud-wall","kind":"staple","positionMm":{"x":-835,"y":-500,"z":-65},"tool":null}] --tailsMm.a 400 --tailsMm.b 200 --tool.id tool.veltmark-dc-8 --tool.version 1
cable.add --a.entity 7 --a.entry clamp-bottom-1 --b.entity 8 --b.entry clamp-bottom-1 --lengthMm 1591 --ref.id cable.sorrelby-nmb-14-2 --ref.version 1 --route [{"entity":null,"fixture":"stud-wall","kind":"staple","positionMm":{"x":-835,"y":-1000,"z":-65},"tool":null},{"entity":null,"fixture":"stud-wall","kind":"bore","positionMm":{"x":-449,"y":-1000,"z":-65},"tool":{"id":"tool.corriden-sa-12","version":1}},{"entity":null,"fixture":"stud-wall","kind":"staple","positionMm":{"x":-63,"y":-1000,"z":-65},"tool":null}] --tailsMm.a 200 --tailsMm.b 200 --tool.id tool.veltmark-dc-8 --tool.version 1
# 7. The jackets stripped with the NM stripper: 300 of the panel's 400 mm tail, 150 of each box's 200.
cable.strip --end a --id 1 --jacketMm 300 --tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-nm12 --tool.version 1
cable.strip --end b --id 1 --jacketMm 150 --tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-nm12 --tool.version 1
cable.strip --end a --id 2 --jacketMm 150 --tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-nm12 --tool.version 1
cable.strip --end b --id 2 --jacketMm 150 --tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-nm12 --tool.version 1
# 8. In the panel: cable 1's black, white and bare on the blocks' bottom clamps, stripped 9 mm (the
#    blocks' marked strip) through the NM stripper's 14 AWG solid hole, torqued to their marked 0.6 N.m
#    with the 0.3-1.2 N.m torque screwdriver.
wire.land --at.entity 4 --at.terminal b --at.termination.accessory null --at.termination.clamp.tool.id tool.calderyn-ts-03 --at.termination.clamp.tool.version 1 --at.termination.clamp.torqueNm 0.6 --at.termination.method screw --at.termination.strip.hole sol14 --at.termination.strip.lengthMm 9 --at.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-nm12 --at.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --end a --id 2
wire.land --at.entity 5 --at.terminal b --at.termination.accessory null --at.termination.clamp.tool.id tool.calderyn-ts-03 --at.termination.clamp.tool.version 1 --at.termination.clamp.torqueNm 0.6 --at.termination.method screw --at.termination.strip.hole sol14 --at.termination.strip.lengthMm 9 --at.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-nm12 --at.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --end a --id 3
wire.land --at.entity 6 --at.terminal b --at.termination.accessory null --at.termination.clamp.tool.id tool.calderyn-ts-03 --at.termination.clamp.tool.version 1 --at.termination.clamp.torqueNm 0.6 --at.termination.method screw --at.termination.strip.hole sol14 --at.termination.strip.lengthMm 9 --at.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-nm12 --at.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --end a --id 4
# 9. Wire nuts at the junction box's opening (a nut has no mount, and nothing but a mounted device may
#    be placed inside a box's body: F3.5): two large ones (9 black, 10 white), a small one (11 bare).
#    Each conductor stripped 13 mm through the 14 AWG solid hole and twisted on (no tool, no torque).
entity.place --inEntry null --mountedOn null --orientationMdeg.pitch 0 --orientationMdeg.roll 0 --orientationMdeg.yaw 0 --positionMm.x -830 --positionMm.y -830 --positionMm.z 55 --ref.id splice.corvelle-tw-l --ref.version 1
entity.place --inEntry null --mountedOn null --orientationMdeg.pitch 0 --orientationMdeg.roll 0 --orientationMdeg.yaw 0 --positionMm.x -800 --positionMm.y -830 --positionMm.z 55 --ref.id splice.corvelle-tw-l --ref.version 1
entity.place --inEntry null --mountedOn null --orientationMdeg.pitch 0 --orientationMdeg.roll 0 --orientationMdeg.yaw 0 --positionMm.x -768 --positionMm.y -830 --positionMm.z 55 --ref.id splice.corvelle-tw-s --ref.version 1
wire.land --at.entity 9 --at.terminal splice --at.termination.accessory null --at.termination.clamp.tool null --at.termination.clamp.torqueNm null --at.termination.method twistOn --at.termination.strip.hole sol14 --at.termination.strip.lengthMm 13 --at.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-nm12 --at.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --end b --id 2
wire.land --at.entity 9 --at.terminal splice --at.termination.accessory null --at.termination.clamp.tool null --at.termination.clamp.torqueNm null --at.termination.method twistOn --at.termination.strip.hole sol14 --at.termination.strip.lengthMm 13 --at.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-nm12 --at.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --end a --id 5
wire.land --at.entity 10 --at.terminal splice --at.termination.accessory null --at.termination.clamp.tool null --at.termination.clamp.torqueNm null --at.termination.method twistOn --at.termination.strip.hole sol14 --at.termination.strip.lengthMm 13 --at.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-nm12 --at.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --end b --id 3
wire.land --at.entity 10 --at.terminal splice --at.termination.accessory null --at.termination.clamp.tool null --at.termination.clamp.torqueNm null --at.termination.method twistOn --at.termination.strip.hole sol14 --at.termination.strip.lengthMm 13 --at.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-nm12 --at.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --end a --id 6
wire.land --at.entity 11 --at.terminal splice --at.termination.accessory null --at.termination.clamp.tool null --at.termination.clamp.torqueNm null --at.termination.method twistOn --at.termination.strip.hole sol14 --at.termination.strip.lengthMm 13 --at.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-nm12 --at.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --end b --id 4
wire.land --at.entity 11 --at.terminal splice --at.termination.accessory null --at.termination.clamp.tool null --at.termination.clamp.torqueNm null --at.termination.method twistOn --at.termination.strip.hole sol14 --at.termination.strip.lengthMm 13 --at.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-nm12 --at.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --end a --id 7
# 10. The 120 V 60 W lamp (12) on the lamp box's opening: black on screw a, white on screw b, stripped
#     16 mm (its marked strip), torqued to its marked 1.8 N.m with the 1-5 N.m torque screwdriver. The
#     bare EGC (wire 7) stays folded back at the lamp box: the keyless holder has no grounding
#     terminal, and the stand-in supply none either (P3 has no grounding rules; P4 bonds it).
entity.place --inEntry null --mountedOn null --orientationMdeg.pitch 0 --orientationMdeg.roll 0 --orientationMdeg.yaw 0 --positionMm.x -165 --positionMm.y -850 --positionMm.z 55 --ref.id lamp.lumivane-120v-60w --ref.version 1
wire.land --at.entity 12 --at.terminal a --at.termination.accessory null --at.termination.clamp.tool.id tool.calderyn-ts-15 --at.termination.clamp.tool.version 1 --at.termination.clamp.torqueNm 1.8 --at.termination.method screw --at.termination.strip.hole sol14 --at.termination.strip.lengthMm 16 --at.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-nm12 --at.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --end b --id 5
wire.land --at.entity 12 --at.terminal b --at.termination.accessory null --at.termination.clamp.tool.id tool.calderyn-ts-15 --at.termination.clamp.tool.version 1 --at.termination.clamp.torqueNm 1.8 --at.termination.method screw --at.termination.strip.hole sol14 --at.termination.strip.lengthMm 16 --at.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-nm12 --at.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --end b --id 6
# 11. The supply conductors last (the stand-in has no disconnect), in through ko-bottom-1: L1 (wire 8)
#     up past the breaker's right side and down onto its line screw, N (wire 9) to the neutral block's
#     top clamp; stripped 13 mm with the general stripper, the service and breaker screws torqued to
#     4 N.m, the block to 0.6 N.m.
wire.add --a.entity 1 --a.terminal l1 --a.termination.accessory null --a.termination.clamp.tool.id tool.calderyn-ts-15 --a.termination.clamp.tool.version 1 --a.termination.clamp.torqueNm 4 --a.termination.method screw --a.termination.strip.hole sol14 --a.termination.strip.lengthMm 13 --a.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-1018 --a.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --b.entity 3 --b.terminal line --b.termination.accessory null --b.termination.clamp.tool.id tool.calderyn-ts-15 --b.termination.clamp.tool.version 1 --b.termination.clamp.torqueNm 4 --b.termination.method screw --b.termination.strip.hole sol14 --b.termination.strip.lengthMm 13 --b.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-1018 --b.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --colour.base black --colour.stripe null --lengthMm 1363 --ref.id conductor.tallowmere-thhn-14-solid --ref.version 1 --route [{"entity":null,"fixture":null,"kind":"free","positionMm":{"x":-910,"y":700,"z":79},"tool":null},{"entity":null,"fixture":null,"kind":"free","positionMm":{"x":-910,"y":860,"z":79},"tool":null},{"entity":null,"fixture":null,"kind":"free","positionMm":{"x":-840,"y":900,"z":79},"tool":null},{"entity":null,"fixture":null,"kind":"free","positionMm":{"x":-840,"y":1240,"z":79},"tool":null},{"entity":null,"fixture":null,"kind":"free","positionMm":{"x":-920,"y":1240,"z":21},"tool":null}] --tool.id tool.veltmark-dc-8 --tool.version 1
wire.add --a.entity 1 --a.terminal n --a.termination.accessory null --a.termination.clamp.tool.id tool.calderyn-ts-15 --a.termination.clamp.tool.version 1 --a.termination.clamp.torqueNm 4 --a.termination.method screw --a.termination.strip.hole sol14 --a.termination.strip.lengthMm 13 --a.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-1018 --a.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --b.entity 5 --b.terminal a --b.termination.accessory null --b.termination.clamp.tool.id tool.calderyn-ts-03 --b.termination.clamp.tool.version 1 --b.termination.clamp.torqueNm 0.6 --b.termination.method screw --b.termination.strip.hole sol14 --b.termination.strip.lengthMm 9 --b.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-1018 --b.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --colour.base white --colour.stripe null --lengthMm 945 --ref.id conductor.tallowmere-thhn-14-solid --ref.version 1 --route [{"entity":null,"fixture":null,"kind":"free","positionMm":{"x":-900,"y":700,"z":79},"tool":null},{"entity":null,"fixture":null,"kind":"free","positionMm":{"x":-900,"y":860,"z":79},"tool":null},{"entity":null,"fixture":null,"kind":"free","positionMm":{"x":-810,"y":1030,"z":79},"tool":null}] --tool.id tool.veltmark-dc-8 --tool.version 1
# 12. The heater element (13) on the floor in front of the junction box, and two THHN leads (wires 10
#     black, 11 white) from the black and white nuts (a third conductor in each large nut) to its
#     pressure-plate screws: stripped 10 mm (its marked strip), torqued to its marked 1.8 N.m.
entity.place --inEntry null --mountedOn null --orientationMdeg.pitch 0 --orientationMdeg.roll 0 --orientationMdeg.yaw 0 --positionMm.x -1000 --positionMm.y -1200 --positionMm.z 150 --ref.id heater.hearthvale-120v-1500w --ref.version 1
wire.add --a.entity 9 --a.terminal splice --a.termination.accessory null --a.termination.clamp.tool null --a.termination.clamp.torqueNm null --a.termination.method twistOn --a.termination.strip.hole sol14 --a.termination.strip.lengthMm 13 --a.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-1018 --a.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --b.entity 13 --b.terminal a --b.termination.accessory null --b.termination.clamp.tool.id tool.calderyn-ts-15 --b.termination.clamp.tool.version 1 --b.termination.clamp.torqueNm 1.8 --b.termination.method screw --b.termination.strip.hole sol14 --b.termination.strip.lengthMm 10 --b.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-1018 --b.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --colour.base black --colour.stripe null --lengthMm 396 --ref.id conductor.tallowmere-thhn-14-solid --ref.version 1 --route [] --tool.id tool.veltmark-dc-8 --tool.version 1
wire.add --a.entity 10 --a.terminal splice --a.termination.accessory null --a.termination.clamp.tool null --a.termination.clamp.torqueNm null --a.termination.method twistOn --a.termination.strip.hole sol14 --a.termination.strip.lengthMm 13 --a.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-1018 --a.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --b.entity 13 --b.terminal b --b.termination.accessory null --b.termination.clamp.tool.id tool.calderyn-ts-15 --b.termination.clamp.tool.version 1 --b.termination.clamp.torqueNm 1.8 --b.termination.method screw --b.termination.strip.hole sol14 --b.termination.strip.lengthMm 10 --b.termination.strip.tool.id tool.veltmark-ws-1018 --b.termination.strip.tool.version 1 --colour.base white --colour.stripe null --lengthMm 399 --ref.id conductor.tallowmere-thhn-14-solid --ref.version 1 --route [] --tool.id tool.veltmark-dc-8 --tool.version 1
# 13. The breaker on, and 600 s of sim time.
device.operate --control on --id 3 --value true
sim.step --ticks 600000
world.hash
